BACKGROUND

The application includes:

- @anz-bank-nz/ob-system-authority-moleculer
- An underlying ob-system-authority implementation used internally by the Moleculer library
- @anz-bank-nz/lib-ob-third-party-config-mixin
- A System Authority access-token cache
- A third-party configuration cache

The original defect was caused by a TTL intended as 3600 seconds being passed to a cache implementation that interpreted it as 3600 milliseconds. This caused cache expiry after approximately 3.6 seconds.

The fixed implementation should convert:

3600 seconds → 3,600,000 milliseconds

The System Authority token cache also has a configuration similar to:

systemAuthority.cache.ttlBufferInSeconds = 5

The effective token-cache lifetime should therefore be:

token expires_in minus ttlBufferInSeconds

